1
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten it up and try stepping back, okay?

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone calling out,
on the day after the rain.

3
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,460
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,460
I tried walking only on the black parts.

7
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,060
The self-important politicians and
the aunties with blue eyeshadow too,

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone!

12
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kameari surely Kameari!

13
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:33,000
Everybody, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:40,460
Calamity strikes when
you've forgotten about it.

16
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:47,800
Idiot! You forgot it?

17
00:01:47,940 --> 00:01:48,440
Yes.

18
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:51,680
I told you so many times, and yet you -

19
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:53,500
It hurts! I'm dying!

20
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:55,760
Chief, please calm down.

21
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,660
If your blood pressure rises again,
it'll be bad.

22
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:00,700
Or you might just drop
dead on top of it all.

23
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:01,700
What did you say?

24
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,300
I was joking.

25
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,100
What's wrong?

26
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,680
Sorry. Stomach medicine and water, please.

27
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:10,320
Yes.

28
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:15,960
Ryo-chan, what did you forget?

29
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,240
My residence certificate.

30
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,220
Residence certificate.

31
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:22,980
In the household survey, only Ryotsu
failed to submit his residence certificate.

32
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:26,540
I've been telling him to
bring it for a whole month now.

33
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,140
For a whole month.

34
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:29,300
What's your problem, you two?

35
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:31,980
Chief, I'll definitely bring it tomorrow.

36
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:33,240
Is that a promise?

37
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:36,440
Yes, though lately my
memory has been really bad.

38
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,620
But I'll definitely bring it tomorrow.

39
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,780
Once Ryotsu starts talking,
he never stops at just two words.

40
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:44,740
Not just two, he goes on to
three or four words, and yet...

41
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,780
What are you saying?
I'll definitely bring it tomorrow!

42
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:48,580
Ryo-san.

43
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:51,300
What is it? Do you have a minute?

44
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:52,180
Sure.

45
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:56,333
Actually, I bought advance tickets
for the night racing four days ago,

46
00:02:56,383 --> 00:02:59,028
but then a sudden job came up and
I had to go out to the countryside,

47
00:02:59,078 --> 00:03:00,780
and I only got back last night.

48
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:03,800
I figured you'd know the results, Ryo-san.

49
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:06,660
Is that all? So, which race was it?

50
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,280
Race 10 first, please.

51
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:13,060
In race 10, number 8, the busty gal held on to win,
and it turned into a huge payout.

52
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,660
Seriously? I bet on it at the track.
What about second place?

53
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:20,168
Oyaji Gag Order, ridden by Horiuchi,
who made a late charge.

54
00:03:20,218 --> 00:03:22,300
The 8-2 paid 18,000 yen!

55
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,700
You won that much?

56
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:27,240
Yeah, by the way, I won 10,000 yen's worth.

57
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:30,420
Seriously? That's 1.8 million yen!

58
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:31,300
Yeah, well.

59
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:34,040
So what about the main event, the 11th race?

60
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,040
The main race is...

61
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:37,300
Ryo-san, I suddenly remembered something.

62
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,100
I'll ask you about the
main race results later.

63
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:40,020
See you.

64
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:42,360
What a weird guy.

65
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,846
Just kidding,

66
00:03:43,896 --> 00:03:47,480
I guess I'll get to work.

67
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,040
Ryotsu, where's your forgetfulness?

68
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:56,920
How can you forget things so easily yet
remember the horse race results perfectly?

69
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,440
Chief.

70
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:02,380
Chief, shouldn't you lie down and rest?

71
00:04:02,860 --> 00:04:07,040
Right. Ryotsu, if you forget your
residence certificate tomorrow, you're fired.

72
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:09,660
Yes, I'm fine. Take care.

73
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:12,420
It's this way, grandma.

74
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,820
Good thing I took cup
noodles as my pachinko prize.

75
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:20,320
When you're broke,
that really comes in handy.

76
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,300
Chief, are you feeling better now?

77
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,360
Much better, thanks.

78
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,180
Chief, what do you want to do for lunch?

79
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,760
We're thinking of going
to the new restaurant

80
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,580
that just opened on 3rd Street.

81
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:35,700
But since you should probably keep it light today,
just soba will do,

82
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:36,820
I'll pass.

83
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:38,160
What about you, senior officer?

84
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:40,320
Cup ramen's good enough for me.

85
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,780
That's pretty frugal of you.

86
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:42,880
Mind your own business.

87
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,620
You rich kids

88
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:47,180
don't get to call a commoner's
meal something to look down on.

89
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:51,460
But didn't you get a big sum
of money four or five days ago?

90
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:54,600
Yeah, it was about 1.8 million yen, right?

91
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:57,740
Well, with four days, it's all gone.

92
00:04:57,740 --> 00:04:59,360
In just four days?

93
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,900
Where's the commoner in that?

94
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:01,760
But today is

95
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:06,380
Reiko, that idiot has even
forgotten today is payday.

96
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,580
Looks that way.

97
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:14,000
If we tell him,
he'll spend it all right away.

98
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,260
Let's keep quiet until he remembers on his own,
for his own good.

99
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:17,840
Yes.

100
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:22,960
Thanks for your hard work.

101
00:05:22,960 --> 00:05:24,580
Good work.

102
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:27,540
I hear you're getting married.
Congratulations!

103
00:05:27,540 --> 00:05:29,280
Yes, Chief Ohara.

104
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:30,960
Accounting section chief.

105
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,500
Phew, glad we made it in time.

106
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:33,900
Is there something I can do for you?

107
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,720
Could you give this to Ryotsu for me?

108
00:05:37,260 --> 00:05:38,880
Isn't this his pay envelope?

109
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,680
I tried to transfer Ryotsu's
salary into his account,

110
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,700
but his account had been closed,
so I couldn't.

111
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:46,540
What a hopeless guy.

112
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:49,300
Understood. I'll hand it to him myself.

113
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:52,660
Well, I'll also need proof
that he received it himself.

114
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:56,040
Please tell Ryotsu to
bring his seal tomorrow.

115
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,660
Yes, understood.

116
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:03,160
Chief-san, Ryo-chan,
it's a phone call for you.

117
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:07,300
Hello? I'm off duty now, so what is it?

118
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:07,740
Shut up.

119
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:10,500
You're always off duty anyway, aren't you?

120
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:11,980
Don't say that!

121
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:15,200
Chief, if you get this worked up,
a blood vessel is going to burst.

122
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,320
Shut up!

123
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,660
Listen! Tomorrow, bring your seal
along with your residence certificate!

124
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,760
Seal? Why do I need a seal?

125
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:25,140
It's important for you!
Don't you dare forget!

126
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,340
What a troublesome guy you are.

127
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,420
That was a nice bath.

128
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,960
Dad, I'll get you a beer.

129
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:39,040
Here you go.
Thanks for your hard work again today.

130
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:40,660
Thanks.

131
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:48,440
Beer after a bath really is the best.

132
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:52,180
Dad, you really do look
like you're enjoying that.

133
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:56,200
Beer poured by Mom is extra special.

134
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,680
Dad, just...

135
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,780
What's wrong?

136
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:06,440
I've got a feeling I
forgot something important.

137
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:10,360
Oh my, Dad, haven't you been
forgetting things a lot lately?

138
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:13,000
Don't be silly, I'm not like Ryotsu.

139
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,500
That's it, it's probably about Ryotsu!

140
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,500
Yeah! It's Ryotsu!

141
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:23,520
Why do I have to think about
that guy even after I get home?

142
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,400
The beer's starting to taste bad.

143
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:29,020
If you can't remember it,
it can't be that important, can it?

144
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,400
But I remembered it clearly in the bath.

145
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:32,920
Right.

146
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:36,520
Right! I'll go back in the
bath and try to remember again.

147
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,420
You've been drinking beer,
are you sure you're alright?

148
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:40,700
I'm fine!

149
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:43,600
You're just too earnest, you know.

150
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:48,660
Ryo, s-, that is, money, money...

151
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:52,000
I-I remember! It's the pay envelope!

152
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:55,460
Damn it! You went and ruined my good mood!

153
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,780
So we just hand over his pay, right?

154
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:05,780
What a flag-wavingly troublesome guy he is.

155
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:06,920
Is that so?

156
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:13,920
How can you eat ramen
first thing in the morning?

157
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:17,680
And he's been eating it three
times a day for the past week.

158
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,440
Shut up.

159
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,560
It can't be helped, it's before payday.

160
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,620
What are you learning?

161
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:25,280
Don't just suddenly show up like that.

162
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,920
Honestly,
what a noisy man first thing in the morning.

163
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:36,560
Senpai, are you all right?

164
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:40,280
Ryotsu,
did you bring your residence certificate?

165
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:43,340
Damn, sorry, I forgot again.

166
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:44,920
Then your seal?

167
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,200
Seal? That's the first I've heard of it.

168
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,700
I told you on the phone yesterday evening,
didn't I?

169
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,140
Did you?

170
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:55,420
Why do you always forget
as soon as I tell you?

171
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:57,700
Sorry, tomorrow I'll definitely -

172
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:58,460
Wait.

173
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,520
I'll write it down for you, so don't forget.

174
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:05,080
But knowing you, Ryo-chan,
you'll lose the paper.

175
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,480
Yeah, you're right.

176
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,560
Don't worry, I absolutely won't lose it.

177
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,760
I can't trust -

178
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:10,220
Come on, that's -

179
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:11,660
Right.

180
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,840
W-what are you -

181
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,880
Hold still.

182
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,800
W-what are you doing? Stop it, please!

183
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:26,980
Shut up and stay still.

184
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:28,200
Ow

185
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:30,220
There, that should do it.

186
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:32,020
What do you think you're doing?

187
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,920
There was a staircase like this,
wasn't there?

188
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:36,840
But does Ryo-chan even
have a mirror in his room?

189
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:39,920
Even if he did,
I don't think Ryo-chan would look at it.

190
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:41,260
Yeah, I see.

191
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:44,000
Right, I'll write it here too.
There, that's done.

192
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,020
It'll probably wash off
if he takes a bath, though.

193
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,460
Don't worry,
he won't bathe for about a week.

194
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,440
Right.

195
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,820
Still worried

196
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:55,540
That's right.

197
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,840
This is a forgetting prevention machine.

198
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:01,160
What part of this is a machine?

199
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:03,380
My grandson made it at kindergarten.

200
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,100
I'll lend this to you.

201
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:06,180
Use it carefully.

202
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:08,500
Something that important?

203
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:09,720
No, I'll decline.

204
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,700
Don't say that.

205
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,800
Write down the things you're
likely to forget like this,

206
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,800
and as you check each one, press its button.

207
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,680
Press them all and nothing gets forgotten.

208
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,120
Pretty well made, isn't it?

209
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:22,060
It's the perfect machine for you.

210
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,880
So, I just change the parts
that say handkerchief and such

211
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:27,300
to seal or residence certificate, right?

212
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:30,280
What do you mean,
"so"? Do you think I'm a kindergartner?

213
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:33,540
What was it again?

214
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,400
Chief, what's wrong?

215
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:39,200
I feel like something
important happened today.

216
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,940
See? Even the Chief has forgotten.

217
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:44,420
Or shall I lend you this machine?

218
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:46,700
Shut up. Don't lump me in with you.

219
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,560
Mine is just doorway forgetting.

220
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:52,220
I remembered when I walked
into the police box, though.

221
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:56,060
Then shouldn't we recreate the same situation
as when you walked into the police box?

222
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:59,940
Yes, the memory might suddenly come back.

223
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:02,740
Come to think of it,
I remembered that way yesterday too.

224
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,160
Then let's recreate it.

225
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:07,120
I'm pretty sure I was taking
a map out of the bookshelf.

226
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:11,440
I was carrying tea,
and Ryo-chan was eating cup ramen.

227
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:13,200
Hey, are you planning to
make me eat that again?

228
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,920
We have to recreate
the exact same situation.

229
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:19,000
I'll go make it. Ryo-chan, sit at your desk.

230
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:20,960
Here we go.

231
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,940
All set and ready.

232
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:25,480
Then let's begin.

233
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,200
Okay.

234
00:11:27,820 --> 00:11:30,580
How can you eat ramen
this early in the morning?

235
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:32,860
Hey, you're the one who told me to eat it!

236
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:35,420
Ryo-chan, it's acting, don't forget.

237
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:36,600
Yeah, got it.

238
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:42,180
I'm pretty sure when I came to this spot,
Ryotsu was throwing up his ramen.

239
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:43,960
Senpai, please throw up.

240
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:46,700
Ryo-chan.

241
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:47,880
Yes.

242
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:53,460
If you put this much pepper in,
you'll choke and throw up for sure.

243
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:54,780
Just you wait, Reiko.

244
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,260
Okay, once more.

245
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:58,260
Fine, I'll eat it, I'll eat it.

246
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,600
I'm starting to remember up to about here.

247
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,100
Just a little more, Reiko-kun.

248
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:11,500
Yes.

249
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:25,360
So what?

250
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,320
Actually,

251
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,540
you've been leaving me hanging like this,

252
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:29,360
Ryotsu!

253
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:34,120
Actually, I picked up your pay envelope
from the accounting chief yesterday.

254
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,420
My pay envelope?

255
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:37,720
Pay envelope?

256
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,760
Payday was yesterday?

257
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,660
Only realizing it now.

258
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:45,000
What an idiot.

259
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:45,420
Fumi-chan!

260
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:49,060
Hurry up and give me back my pay envelope,
Fumi-chan!

261
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,240
Alright, alright, don't get so worked up.

262
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,460
I'm handing it over now.

263
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:57,070
It's not here...

264
00:12:57,120 --> 00:13:00,320
It was definitely here
until we got to the station.

265
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:15,240
Chief, what's wrong?
Hurry up and give me my pay!

266
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:21,260
I'd love to hand it over, but I need
your seal as proof that you received it.

267
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:23,440
So that's why you kept saying seal.

268
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,440
I'll bring it right away.

269
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:29,660
Damn, what am I supposed to do?

270
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:31,200
The pay. The pay envelope.

271
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:36,920
I had it right up to the precinct, though.

272
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,300
That's it. It might be in my suit pocket.

273
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,100
I just remembered something.

274
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,220
I'm heading to the precinct,
so take over for me.

275
00:13:43,220 --> 00:13:43,500
Yes.

276
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:46,140
Why did the Chief suddenly
start acting like this?

277
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:46,800
San.

278
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,280
Not here, not here, not here...

279
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:57,520
Not here.

280
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:02,220
Did I drop it on the way to the police box?

281
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:02,900
That's it!

282
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:05,480
Let's ask the lost property office.

283
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:10,240
You were quick.

284
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:12,960
Why don't we have lunch together now?

285
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,680
Rather, about my pay...

286
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:17,120
You're being unsociable, Ryotsu.

287
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:17,860
Yeah.

288
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:19,760
I'll treat you, so let's have some eel.

289
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:20,420
Eel...?

290
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:23,240
Weren't we having soba
because your stomach was bad?

291
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:25,020
No, it's better now.

292
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:30,420
When the suspicious chief suddenly turns kind,
he always has an ulterior motive.

293
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:36,020
What are you talking about? I invited you because I
couldn't stand watching you eat nothing but ramen every day.

294
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:41,620
I eat ramen every month before payday.
In the worst times, I've had only water.

295
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:43,540
But the chief has never once...

296
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:48,780
What are you talking about? As your superior,
I'm inviting you out of concern for your health.

297
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,340
Come on, let's go, let's go!

298
00:14:54,340 --> 00:14:56,120
Have you decided on your order?

299
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,500
Eel, the regular one.

300
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:59,700
Little old me wants the top-grade one,
you know.

301
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:00,760
What?

302
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,960
If you don't want to be treated,
you don't have to be.

303
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,100
I'll pay out of my own salary.

304
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:07,860
So hand over my pay already.

305
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:11,760
I didn't say it because
I didn't want to treat you.

306
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,940
After all, you ate so much ramen.

307
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:17,000
I just thought the regular
would be about right.

308
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,640
As for that order...

309
00:15:20,340 --> 00:15:21,080
If I dropped it, that'd be bad.

310
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,160
Very well.

311
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:23,700
Just like that, you're treating us?

312
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:25,500
Now I'm even more suspicious.

313
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:28,600
Splurging once in a while isn't bad.

314
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:32,080
Don't tell me you blew my salary.

315
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:35,000
No, being serious is Chief
Ohara's only redeeming quality.

316
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:35,680
No way.

317
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:38,740
So did I forget the pay envelope at home?

318
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,700
Or did I drop it?

319
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:40,420
Phew.

320
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:44,260
What, you're staring at my face?

321
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:44,980
No.

322
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:46,640
Lately, the Chief's gotten more wrinkles,

323
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:48,240
so I was thinking you're getting old.

324
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:52,220
When you have subordinates like you,
the worry ages a man.

325
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,460
I suppose so.

326
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:58,860
But as you get older, you must forget
and lose things more often, right?

327
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:01,940
What are you talking about? That's nonsense.

328
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:03,380
Thank you for waiting.

329
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:06,420
Good work. Come on, let's eat.

330
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:08,360
Well then, I'll dig in.

331
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:12,840
Looks like I hit the nail right on the head.

332
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,480
Chief, thank you for the meal.

333
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,800
A café way out here?

334
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,300
Little me is getting a
craving for coffee now.

335
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:24,780
I don't want any.

336
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,120
I see.

337
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:28,600
Then I'll go drink it by myself.

338
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:29,900
Chief, give me my pay.

339
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:32,500
Now I want coffee too.

340
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:36,980
There's no doubt about it now.

341
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,660
Two of your most expensive Blue Mountains.

342
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:43,660
I'll just have the blend.

343
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:45,560
Chief, little old me will treat you.

344
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:47,460
Two Blue Mountains.

345
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:53,680
Oh dear. Ryotsu,
did you notice I don't have your pay on me?

346
00:16:54,060 --> 00:17:02,880
Chief... Reiko-kun, senpai, weren't we supposed to eat at that new restaurant today?
But there was a huge line.

347
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:09,560
so we gave up. That's a shame.
Alright, I'll treat you all here. What?

348
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:17,880
Why are you so surprised? These guys look after me all the time, so as a senior I should treat them once in a while.
It's kind of creepy, isn't it?

349
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,300
I'd better decline.
I'm scared of what comes later.

350
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:23,480
Never mind, never mind. Can't you
just accept the gesture graciously?

351
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:27,220
Then, Chief,
please pay for it out of my salary.

352
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:32,140
This guy's totally figured out
that I lost his pay envelope.

353
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:33,500
Uh-oh.

354
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:34,300
That's right.

355
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,240
Reiko, Nakagawa!

356
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:38,620
I'm going to have some Blue
Mountain treated to me too.

357
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:41,060
Don't hold back. Accept the treat.

358
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,760
Four.

359
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:48,140
I'll pay your salary, but I'm deducting
the cost of the treat, so there.

360
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:51,540
Chief, you didn't have my pay on you,
did you?

361
00:17:51,540 --> 00:17:54,220
What are you talking about?
I've got it, of course.

362
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,180
What's with this confident attitude?

363
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:57,800
Damn it!

364
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:01,280
Fine, fine.
Then hurry up and hand over my pay.

365
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:07,820
I'll give it to you, but if there's something you want to buy,
write the item, the amount, and the reason on a form and submit it.

366
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:09,980
Then I'll hand it over each time.

367
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,460
W-what are you talking about?

368
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:14,240
Why do I have to do something like that?

369
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:17,840
Starting today,
I'll manage your salary for you.

370
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,720
You're not serious, are you?

371
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,560
Shut up.

372
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:24,400
This is your own fault for losing
your bank account in the first place.

373
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:27,920
If I'm the one managing it,
on the payment day for utility bills,

374
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:31,140
the account balance will
never end up at zero.

375
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:32,580
That's a good idea.

376
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:36,260
If the Chief manages it,
you might even be able to save some money.

377
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:38,380
Don't you two go adding
your own nonsense too.

378
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:39,720
Damn it.

379
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,560
Chief, it's done. I've finished it.

380
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,740
This is what I want right now.

381
00:18:47,740 --> 00:18:48,660
Let's see.

382
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:51,260
Radio-controlled airplane engine,
20,000 yen.

383
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:52,920
Pachinko money, 50,000 yen.

384
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,100
Drinking money, 20,000 yen.

385
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:55,980
Video game software, 5,000 yen.

386
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:59,300
No way. I can't approve this nonsense.

387
00:18:59,300 --> 00:19:00,520
What are you doing?

388
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:02,960
Buy something that's good for you.

389
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:04,580
You'll have to buy it all again.

390
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:07,160
You reject everything when I write it properly,
you know.

391
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:08,920
Right, then,

392
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,340
Chief, please.

393
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,900
You did write it properly this time,
didn't you?

394
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:14,240
Yes, of course.

395
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:18,380
A Benz, an apartment, land.

396
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:22,220
What are you thinking?

397
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:25,100
It's something useful, isn't it?
For the future.

398
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:28,340
Where do you expect 32
million yen to come from?

399
00:19:28,340 --> 00:19:31,640
It's an advance on my salary,
up to about ten years from now.

400
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:34,720
Don't be ridiculous!
Only buy what you need to live.

401
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:36,620
Damn it, seriously.

402
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,100
Alright then.

403
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:41,360
What's this?

404
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:42,880
I rewrote it.

405
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:44,620
There's this many?

406
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:47,140
It's probably all useless junk again,
isn't it?

407
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:48,720
It's a Bible, right?

408
00:19:48,720 --> 00:19:49,960
What do you plan to do with it?

409
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,560
Of course I'll read it.

410
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,360
Liar.

411
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:54,180
There's no way you'd ever read it.

412
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:55,360
That's prejudice.

413
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,940
Prejudice? Don't be ridiculous.
Ken Shimura, Ken Takakura, whatever!

414
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,060
Chief, please calm down.

415
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:02,460
It's cruel to judge him by his appearance.

416
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:03,340
That's right.

417
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:05,980
If it's a Bible, I don't think
there's any harm in having one.

418
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:08,120
You sly one!

419
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,140
What is this "Amida Nyorai" thing?

420
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:16,200
I'm interested in the mind of the Buddha,
so I'd really like one.

421
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:19,220
Even though you always say
there's no such thing as gods,

422
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,720
I do believe in Buddha.

423
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:22,280
Anyway, isn't it expensive?

424
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:24,380
What, 8,000 yen for a three-shot one?

425
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:28,220
Your brain's worth about 30 yen,
and yet this is too expensive, isn't it?

426
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:31,040
I was hoping a charismatic
barber would buy it for me.

427
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:32,840
What charismatic?

428
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:35,820
Your head's good enough with my clippers.

429
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:39,120
No, this won't do. No, this won't do.
No, this won't do. None of these will do.

430
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:41,500
There, I've looked over all of it.
Take it back over there.

431
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,020
So you okayed everything, then?

432
00:20:43,020 --> 00:20:46,180
Don't talk nonsense.
I'll only approve this one.

433
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:48,440
Hurry up and take it.

434
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:50,160
What's this?

435
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,040
It's the money for what I approved.

436
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:54,080
At this rate, you can't even buy a Bible.

437
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,940
You won't read it anyway,
so go look for one at a used bookstore.

438
00:20:56,940 --> 00:20:59,320
Even Lord Amida costs
around 200,000 yen, surely.

439
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:02,060
If you buy one of those plastic model kits you're so good at,
it's cheap.

440
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:04,980
Of course there's no
plastic model of Amida Nyorai!

441
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,020
That's all!

442
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:08,880
Come on, this is school, after all.

443
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:12,580
What can you possibly do
with 1,000 yen these days?

444
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:16,880
It's all this bank's fault to begin with.

445
00:21:17,640 --> 00:21:19,260
I'm going to give them a piece of my mind.

446
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,740
Are you recommending
a comprehensive account?

447
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:32,340
Well, another day's over, I suppose.

448
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:40,380
So you actually bought that Bible?

449
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:42,440
Never mind that, just look at this.

450
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,380
The benefits of a comprehensive account.

451
00:21:44,380 --> 00:21:47,820
If you open a comprehensive account,
you build up a monthly savings fund,

452
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:50,700
and when your account lacks
the balance for utility bills,

453
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:53,600
the savings can cover the payments for you.

454
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,800
That's convenient.

455
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:58,060
I'll open a comprehensive account.

456
00:21:58,060 --> 00:22:01,500
So I won't need the Chief
managing my money anymore.

457
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:03,900
So that's your angle.

458
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,380
Ryotsu, care to join me for a drink tonight?

459
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,560
No, thanks.

460
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,420
Don't be so stiff about it.

461
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:12,200
Come on, let's take our time and talk.

462
00:22:13,320 --> 00:22:15,260
It's been a tough day, hasn't it?

463
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:16,800
How about some sushi?

464
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,140
Never mind all that,
just give me back my pay.

465
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,200
Senpai.

466
00:22:24,860 --> 00:22:25,980
It's Honda.

467
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:30,140
W-what's going on, Chief Ohara?
Are you with senpai or something?

468
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:33,260
Well, I suppose I should look
after my subordinates now and then.

469
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:34,940
Wow, lucky you, senpai.

470
00:22:34,940 --> 00:22:37,980
He said he'd decline, but he won't listen.

471
00:22:37,980 --> 00:22:40,100
Even senpai is going to hold back?

472
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:43,420
Right, senpai, you can't do that!

473
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:45,760
You forgot your important pay envelope.

474
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:48,640
My pay envelope!

475
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:50,880
It's Honda!

476
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:51,720
No doubt about it!

477
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:55,100
Why do you have Ryotsu's pay envelope?

478
00:22:55,580 --> 00:22:59,160
Lost property asked me to
deliver it to you, senpai.

479
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:04,700
Yes, I heard it was left on the
table in the locker room this morning.

480
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:07,780
On the table in the locker room?

481
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:12,420
I took out the pay envelope in
the locker room this morning,

482
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:15,420
set it beside my bag, and then
changed clothes without picking it up.

483
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:19,040
So you just left it sitting on the table.

484
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:19,880
Buchuu

485
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:24,140
for the station-wide lost property
recovery rate survey experiment,

486
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:26,480
we used your salary.

487
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:29,480
Just as I thought,
the officers here are honest people.

488
00:23:31,140 --> 00:23:34,480
Well, that's good. I think it was just a forgotten item,
after all.

489
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,380
What are you saying, Ryotsu-kun?

490
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:39,320
Something about this
feels kind of dangerous.

491
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:42,700
You two might want to use this

492
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:43,580
Seriously.

493
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:44,660
W-what is this?

494
00:23:44,660 --> 00:23:45,980
Well then, see you tomorrow.

495
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:50,540
Chief! Chief! What about the sake and sushi?

496
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:53,940
Your pay's back, so go on your own.

497
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:57,880
Until you pay me back, I'll chase
you to the ends of death, you hear?

498
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:05,520
Kicked the alarm clock awake,
my little toe, ow ow

499
00:24:07,340 --> 00:24:13,900
Drew on my eyebrows for now,
then dash to the station, dash, dash, dash.

500
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:19,300
Main train, a quick once-over,
painting over the housework on my back.

501
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:25,840
Thanks for your hard work this week,
and the overwork is only natural.

502
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:33,180
Though I'm making do with one hand,
the beef bowl's cloudy and extra saucy.

503
00:24:33,840 --> 00:24:40,220
Overtime-day frustrations,
all cleared up neatly with more frustration.

504
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:49,980
Every day is no problem,
once you pass through the hot shower

505
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:56,600
Every day is no-brain,
my energy restored by a sleep pillow

506
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:06,200
Every day is no-brain, I love a girl like me

507
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:13,040
Every day is no-brain,
a Monday with hearts flying around

508
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:17,320
